WEBVTT

00:00.450 --> 00:02.871
Welcome to SysNDD.

00:03.004 --> 00:07.096
Let's put it side by side with other curation resources.

00:07.417 --> 00:10.803
How does SysNDD compare with other gene lists

00:10.937 --> 00:13.512
for neurodevelopmental disorders, or NDDs?

00:13.645 --> 00:20.059
You learn which genes the lists share,
which lists are most alike,

00:20.192 --> 00:22.821
and what a missing gene means.

00:23.117 --> 00:27.440
In the Analyses menu, select Compare curations.

00:27.574 --> 00:31.437
The page is public, so you don't need an account.

00:31.750 --> 00:36.805
Here you see SysNDD next to other curated gene lists.

00:36.939 --> 00:40.739
The badge shows
when the external lists were last refreshed.

00:40.872 --> 00:43.062
Three tabs give three views:

00:43.195 --> 00:46.229
Overlap, Similarity and Table.

00:46.550 --> 00:49.071
Overlap opens with three lists:

00:49.205 --> 00:53.351
SysNDD, PanelApp and Gene2Phenotype.

00:53.485 --> 00:57.678
Each column of the UpSet plot
is one combination of lists,

00:57.812 --> 00:59.774
marked by the dots below.

00:59.908 --> 01:04.588
Its bar counts the genes
that all lists in that column contain.

01:04.722 --> 01:07.877
A column with one dot counts the whole list.

01:08.010 --> 01:13.270
The last column holds
the genes that all three lists share.

01:13.583 --> 01:16.541
Select Add Sources, then SFARI.

01:16.674 --> 01:19.731
The plot redraws with four lists.

01:20.050 --> 01:24.256
SFARI, the Simons Foundation Autism Research Initiative,

01:24.390 --> 01:26.527
collects genes for autism.

01:26.660 --> 01:31.259
Its own column, with one dot, counts every SFARI gene.

01:31.393 --> 01:34.487
The column with four dots is much shorter.

01:34.621 --> 01:40.754
Definitive Only keeps, for each list,
the genes mapped to Definitive.

01:41.050 --> 01:45.515
Similarity shows one cell
for each pair of the eight lists.

01:45.649 --> 01:51.115
Each value is a cosine similarity, from 0.0, no overlap,

01:51.249 --> 01:54.024
to 1.0, identical lists.

01:54.158 --> 01:58.386
PanelApp and Gene2Phenotype are the most similar pair.

01:58.519 --> 02:03.530
SFARI focuses on autism, so its row is the lightest.

02:03.850 --> 02:09.262
Point to a cell:
its value and the two lists appear below the matrix.

02:09.395 --> 02:13.850
The value reflects shared genes, not categories.

02:14.150 --> 02:19.665
Table has a row for each gene;
here it is filtered to one gene, <i>ASPA</i>.

02:19.798 --> 02:23.959
Each list's rating is mapped to the SysNDD categories.

02:24.092 --> 02:30.159
A green check means Definitive,
as in SysNDD, Gene2Phenotype and PanelApp.

02:30.293 --> 02:34.311
SFARI shows an empty circle: not listed.

02:34.617 --> 02:37.449
Not listed is not disagreement.

02:37.582 --> 02:39.818
Lists differ in scope:

02:39.952 --> 02:45.259
SFARI collects autism genes,
PanelApp builds diagnostic panels.

02:45.392 --> 02:49.759
Their inclusion criteria and evidence scales differ too.

02:49.892 --> 02:52.069
Each list is updated at its own pace,

02:52.202 --> 02:56.127
so a new gene may not have been reviewed there yet.

02:56.260 --> 03:00.856
Treat a difference as a lead to check, not as an error.

03:01.150 --> 03:04.429
Remember: Overlap shows shared genes.

03:04.562 --> 03:08.863
Each bar counts the genes
that all lists in its column contain.

03:08.996 --> 03:14.117
Similarity compares which genes are listed,
not their evidence categories.

03:14.250 --> 03:17.004
Not listed is not disagreement.

03:17.137 --> 03:21.951
Check scope, criteria and update date first.

03:22.250 --> 03:27.775
Find Compare curations in the Analyses menu of SysNDD.
